  "nl_text": "The rschema_0087 database is a schema used for a podcasting platform. It contains six tables: User, Podcast, Playlist, User_Publishes_Podcast, User_Creates_Playlist, and Playlist_Contains_Podcasts.\nThe User table contains information about the users of the platform, including their areas of interest, date of birth, email, gender, number of followers, password, user account, user creation time, user description, user ID, and user name. The User_ID column is the primary key.\nThe Podcast table contains information about the podcasts, including the cover image path, creation time, last update time, number of favorites, number of likes, number of visits, podcast file path, podcast ID, podcast name, publisher ID, type, and foreign key to the User table. The Podcast_ID column is the primary key.\nThe Playlist table contains information about the playlists, including the creation time, last update time, number of favorites, number of likes, number of visits, playlist ID, playlist name, playlist path, and user ID who created the playlist. The Playlist_ID column is the primary key.\nThe User_Publishes_Podcast table contains information about which users publish which podcasts, including the podcast ID and user ID. The primary key is a composite key of User_ID and Podcast_ID.\nThe User_Creates_Playlist table contains information about which users create which playlists, including the playlist ID and user ID. The primary key is a composite key of User_ID and Playlist_ID.\nThe Playlist_Contains_Podcasts table contains information about which podcasts are contained in which playlists, including the playlist ID and podcast ID. The primary key is a composite key of Podcast_ID and Playlist_ID.\nIn summary, the rschema_0087 database schema is used to store information about users, podcasts, playlists, and the relationships between them. It includes tables for users, podcasts, playlists, user-podcast relationships, user-playlist relationships, and playlist-podcast relationships.",
  "gold_question": "DevFlix is ​​an innovative audio content sharing platform that aims to provide users with a comprehensive service that integrates podcast publishing, playlist management and audio collection. User information includes username, user account, email, password, user description, gender, interest area, number of followers, number of people following, and user creation time. Podcast information includes publisher, podcast file path, type, podcast name, cover image path, number of visits, number of likes, creation time, number of favorites, and last update time. Playlist information includes the user who created the playlist, the user who created the playlist, playlist name, number of visits, number of likes, creation time, number of favorites, creation time, and last update time. DevFlix allows users to register accounts, publish and manage their own podcasts, interact with other users and create playlists. The platform also provides a collection function, allowing users to save content of interest and access it at any time. In addition, DevFlix also has detailed statistics and analysis functions to track the visit data and user interaction of each podcast and playlist.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0087.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0087\nCREATE TABLE `User` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `date_of_birth` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `areas_of_interest` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `user_description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `followers_count` int(11) DEFAULT 0,\n  `user_creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Podcast` (\n  `podcast_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `podcast_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `podcast_file_path` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `cover_image_path` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `last_update_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `favorites_count` int(11) DEFAULT 0,\n  `likes_count` int(11) DEFAULT 0,\n  `visits_count` int(11) DEFAULT 0,\n  `publisher_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`podcast_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `podcast_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`publisher_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Playlist` (\n  `playlist_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `playlist_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `playlist_path` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `last_update_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `favorites_count` int(11) DEFAULT 0,\n  `likes_count` int(11) DEFAULT 0,\n  `visits_count` int(11) DEFAULT 0,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`playlist_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `playlist_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_Publishes_Podcast` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `podcast_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `podcast_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_publishes_podcast_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_publishes_podcast_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`podcast_id`) REFERENCES `Podcast` (`podcast_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_Creates_Playlist` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `playlist_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `playlist_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_creates_playlist_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_creates_playlist_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`playlist_id`) REFERENCES `Playlist` (`playlist_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Playlist_Contains_Podcasts` (\n  `podcast_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `playlist_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`podcast_id`, `playlist_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `playlist_contains_podcasts_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`podcast_id`) REFERENCES `Podcast` (`podcast_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `playlist_contains_podcasts_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`playlist_id`) REFERENCES `Playlist` (`playlist_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
